  "source": {
    "source_id": "relay-note-01",
    "source_title": "Original teaching note: multiplicative change",
    "source_text": "A percentage change acts on the value at that step. A gain of p percent multiplies the current value by 1 + p/100; a loss of q percent multiplies the current value by 1 - q/100. Successive changes multiply their factors. Adding the percentages is generally not equivalent."
